vcodec/CloseVCodec                                          vcodec/CloseVCodec

   NAME
	CloseVCodec -- The decoder closed, its memory freed - and the frames it still has lent, which may not be shown after.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void CloseVCodec(?*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder)
vcodec/FlushVCodec                                          vcodec/FlushVCodec

   NAME
	FlushVCodec -- Everything sent and not yet handed out forgotten, for a seek: the next packet is a key packet, and the frames lent stay lent.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void FlushVCodec(*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder)
vcodec/GetVCodecInfo                                      vcodec/GetVCodecInfo

   NAME
	GetVCodecInfo -- What the decoder read from the stream, into `info`: 0, or VCERR_NEED_DATA while it has read nothing to say it from.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 GetVCodecInfo(*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder, *vcodec.VCodecInfo info)

   BEHAVIOR
	The size is the pictures' as they are shown, cropped; the rate 0 / 0
	when the stream does not say it. A task will do; it does not wait.
vcodec/OpenVCodec                                            vcodec/OpenVCodec

   NAME
	OpenVCodec -- A decoder for a track, or null and why in `err`: VCERR_NOCODEC when this module cannot decode it here - the board has not its chip, or the codec is not one of its own - VCERR_BUSY when its chip runs no more, VCERR_UNSUPPORTED, VCERR_CORRUPT for a setup it cannot read, VCERR_NOMEMORY.

   SYNOPSIS
	    ?*vcodec.VCodecDecoder OpenVCodec(*const vcodec.VCodecParams params, ?*i32 err)

   BEHAVIOR
	`params` and what it points at are the caller's for the call alone. On a
	process: a chip's decoder may load its firmware.
vcodec/ReceiveVCodecFrame                            vcodec/ReceiveVCodecFrame

   NAME
	ReceiveVCodecFrame -- The next frame in the order frames are shown, into `frame`: 0; VCERR_NEED_DATA when the decoder wants a packet first; VCERR_END after the last frame, once the end was sent; VCERR_UNSUPPORTED for a stream it turns out it cannot decode - before its first frame, the next module is given the track; VCERR_CORRUPT for a picture it stopped on, which it is called again after; VCERR_BUSY with `held` frames lent; VCERR_NOMEMORY.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 ReceiveVCodecFrame(*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder, *videocodec.VideoFrame frame)

   BEHAVIOR
	The frame's planes are the decoder's, lent until ReleaseVCodecFrame, its
	`time` the packet's that made it, its `private` the decoder's.
vcodec/ReleaseVCodecFrame                            vcodec/ReleaseVCodecFrame

   NAME
	ReleaseVCodecFrame -- A frame the decoder lent given back, as ReceiveVCodecFrame filled it in; frames come back in any order.

   SYNOPSIS
	    void ReleaseVCodecFrame(*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder, *videocodec.VideoFrame frame)
vcodec/SendVCodecPacket                                vcodec/SendVCodecPacket

   NAME
	SendVCodecPacket -- A packet of the track in, or its end (VCPKT_END): 0, or VCERR_FULL when it has no room for it yet - a frame is to be taken (ReceiveVCodecFrame) and the packet sent again - or VCERR_NOMEMORY, VCERR_CORRUPT.

   SYNOPSIS
	    i32 SendVCodecPacket(*vcodec.VCodecDecoder decoder, *const vcodec.VCodecPacket packet)

   BEHAVIOR
	The bytes are the caller's for the call alone: the decoder copies what
	it keeps. A packet marked VCPKT_DROP is due before what is shown, and
	may be decoded only as far as later pictures need it.
